  "artists_wikipedia": {
    "Panixphere": {
      "biography": "Panixphere is a British mathcore and experimental punk-rock band associated with the fertile musical circle surrounding Cardiacs. Formed in the 1980s, the group has been led consistently by guitarist and vocalist Christian “Bic” Hayes, while its shifting lineups have included musicians connected with Cardiacs, Levitation, Dark Star, Dragons, and The Wildhearts. Their performances became known for speed, abrasive energy, irregular structures, and a deliberately chaotic edge, placing them in a distinctive position between punk, metal, and avant-garde rock.\n\nPanixphere’s early activity was followed by a 1990s revival featuring Cardiacs members Tim Smith and Jon Poole alongside drummer David Francolini, with the band appearing at prominent British psychedelic and alternative-music events. Although their recorded output was long scarce, Panixphere contributed a Cardiacs cover to the 2010 compilation Leader of the Starry Skies: A Loyal Companion and issued the split release CONFINEMENT/release6 with Spratleys Japs in 2020. Later performances and recordings—including the album Gods & Zeros—have expanded the group’s legacy, documenting a band whose lean, fast, technically intricate music helped connect the Cardiacs tradition to mathcore’s angular intensity.",
      "wikipedia_url": null
    }
