    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Gods And Zeros is the long-awaited debut album by British rock trio Panixphere, released by ATE Music. Built from the band’s history among the Cardiacs, Ring, Levitation, and Dark Star circles, it channels a restless, abrasive energy through jagged guitar, forceful bass, busy drumming, and tightly compressed song structures. The 13-track set moves between punk urgency, ska-tinged rhythms, art-rock eccentricity, and a deliberately unruly sense of humor.\n\nThe album also serves as a document of Panixphere’s distinctive musical lineage, reviving material connected to the group’s earlier live repertoire while presenting it in a fully realized studio form. Tracks such as “Pandy,” “Protocol,” “Perfic / Fiery Flame,” and “More Money Than God” highlight its frantic, unpredictable character, with “Perfic” especially notable as an earlier version of the song later associated with Cardiacs’ “Angleworm Angel.” Critics have emphasized the record’s vitality and its strong connection to the early Cardiacs and Ring aesthetic, making it a significant release for followers of that wider experimental-rock community.",
